    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0080" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9–149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-01T13:00:00+01:00">September 1,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 1—10:02 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3503. Embassy’s despatch 1357, August 17, 1949, transmitting documents re China.
                    Re last paragraph despatch under reference, Strang<anchor n="29" xml:id="d80-f1"
                    /> has now informed me that policy contained in memorandum dated August 15 from
                        FonOff<anchor n="30" xml:id="d80-f2"/> has been approved by Ministers
                    concerned and can be considered official British policy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d80-f1" n="29" xml:id="d80-f1-content">
                <p>Sir William Strang, British Permanent Under Secretary of State for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d80-f2" n="30" xml:id="d80-f2-content">
